ed paths, reducing 614 lines to 198 replacement lines. All persisted verification rows pass on this SHA: normalized non-docstring AST plus directive/shebang identity, focused consumer suite with 270 passed and 1 skipped, path-scoped diff integrity, and worktree make lint plus make typecheck. Comment hygiene and the edited-prose writing-policy scan also pass. The commit carries DCO, canonical ticket trailer, and Change-Id I6eff17cfdcc7f3a30936c2f89449b4c046fb6ea5. The signed execution plan remains certified by file-impact currency. Candidate is not pushed and awaits a non-author exact-SHA semantic and bloat-removal matrix.","timestamp":1789055110607345001}],"created_at":1788570612177512418,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6cf8ab10-7b6e-4850-8eb3-2868c49c74f6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cbd6-ff88-def3-4da7"},{"link_uuid":"be0fa330-2e76-4d8a-9ce7-15d321881b77","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fbe6-b600-30aa-4adc"},{"link_uuid":"7cb2bb82-ecbd-4cc5-b162-d432f3179a7f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7ebe-c6f8-31ec-4fea"},{"link_uuid":"e897113e-b496-4eb0-810b-b20adf0baf1e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0748-e112-19d1-4f6a"},{"link_uuid":"94b8396b-1b21-485e-9eae-346e24b4aa76","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"77e2-9a8c-76e2-4807"},{"link_uuid":"b3f7cd2d-c09f-4e37-9e77-613efde915de","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"db95-1c41-c252-4ddd"},{"link_uuid":"047d2757-db78-4756-956a-51bfd4f76182","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d25f-2fcd-c488-4a50"},{"link_uuid":"21458205-2d67-4dc5-bd5b-23d0d85940d7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8a62-61db-a13e-4317"},{"link_uuid":"76da2f72-3dc8-4ee1-a4a8-03b481ab72b2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d029-0a9a-0ef3-42bd"},{"link_uuid":"f3615b5b-9a50-485d-82ac-8babbcbb8eb9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5dc4-1ccc-51fc-4a73"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nTen developer-tooling files contain repeated, obvious, stale, or historical prose identified by the comment audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`. Several module docstrings are user-facing argparse help and must remain complete.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only comments/docstrings and blank lines in the declared files. Preserve non-docstring AST, test assertions, shebangs, and exact tool/policy directives. Replace history and narration with current operational constraints.\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py` — Describe a bounded deterministic sequence of predetermined REST shapes, not “four calls”; preserve Q1/Q2, project-before-fields ordering, shared readiness, bounded polling/fallback, and evidence on every exit.\n- `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py` — Preserve the post-project precondition, measurement citation, inventory discriminator, bounded fail-closed loop, call-time defaults, and success/failure evidence.\n- `scripts/main_health_report.py` — Preserve scheduled-main purpose, green/red fields, fail-soft last-green lookup, and visible fallback.\n- `scripts/mutation_gate.py` — Preserve sandboxing of clean pytest, the primary mutation run, and survivor reruns; basetemp existence and writable-venv exclusion. Its module docstring is full argparse help; scoped inline comments are source-only.\n- `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py` — Preserve OS isolation, functional probes, two-signal Seatbelt proof, explicit-only waiver, fail-closed policy, and external caution.\n- `scripts/probe_rebar.py` — Preserve the exact bidirectional `show`/lean-list symmetric difference and conditional signature-field intersection.\n- `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py` — Preserve read-only linkage, direct versus inferred metrics, defaults, malformed-record handling, and reproducibility guidance. Its full module docstring is argparse help.\n- `scripts/release_guards.py` — Describe all four guards, including `check_mcp_registry_description`; preserve their distinct return contracts, ancestry behavior, environment protection, 100-character registry-description limit, and publish ordering. Its full module docstring is argparse help.\n- `scripts/retarget_jira_project.py` — Preserve stale binding/snapshot behavior, dry-run/apply, backup and tag stripping, post-preview safety, and the current report/strip help text, including the explanatory block near lines 55–60. Its full module docstring is argparse help.\n- `scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py` — Preserve jobs plus annotations, timeout/cancel distinction, and comment-only/no-vote behavior.\n\nConsumers include argparse help, CI/release workflows, manual Jira operators, mutation infrastructure, tests, and direct imports. Preserve every shebang and exact `noqa`, `type: ignore`, `pragma`, `raw-git-ok:`, and related policy directive.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only comments/docstrings or blank lines in the declared files; executable structure and exact directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked TSV semantic matrix authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row showing that redundant, obvious, duplicated, stale, or historical prose was removed while current rationale remained.\n- [ ] The independent matrix is complete against the exact candidate before the first Gerrit push.\n- [ ] Recorded focused checks pass at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] The path-scoped `git diff --check` passes at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] Worktree-venv `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] Gerrit `Verified +1` supplies the repository-wide suite per operator direction.\n- [ ] Missing or FAIL semantic rows block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded prose-only guards, focused tests, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv `make lint` plus `make typecheck` before push. Complete the independent matrix against the exact candidate before its first Gerrit push. The independent matrix, not exact prose matching, judges semantic preservation. Gerrit `Verified +1` supplies the repository-wide suite.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/main_health_report.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/mutation_gate.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/probe_rebar.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/release_guards.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/retarget_jira_project.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","3de8-31a0-25ef-456d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3de8-31a0-25ef-456d","parent_status_uuid":"a3e54a0c-6924-42a0-89ec-9fff9aa3a86d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"40d7-eca8-8726-4b14","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in scripts — cohort 04: jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe–summarize_ci_failures","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import ast, io, re, subprocess, sys, tokenize\nDIRECTIVE = re.compile(r\"#\\s*(?:noqa\\b|type:\\s*ignore\\b|pragma:\\s*no cover\\b|(?:fmt|isort):\\s*(?:on|off|skip)\\b|pyright:|mypy:|ruff:|pylint:|nosec\\b|coding[:=]|[A-Za-z][\\w-]*-ok:)\", re.I)\nOWNERS = (ast.Module, ast.ClassDef, ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)\ndef src(ref, path):\n    return subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{ref}:{path}\"], text=True)\ndef norm_ast(text):\n    tree = ast.parse(text, type_comments=True)\n    for ti in tree.type_ignores:\n        ti.lineno = 0\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, OWNERS) and node.body and isinstance(node.body[0], ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value, str):\n            node.body = node.body[1:]\n    return ast.dump(tree, include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(text):\n    shebang = text.splitlines()[0] if text.startswith(\"#!\") else \"\"\n    comments = [tok.string for tok in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(text).readline) if tok.type == tokenize.COMMENT and DIRECTIVE.search(tok.string)]\n    return shebang, comments\nbad_ast, bad_directives = [], []\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    before, after = src(\"HEAD^\", path), src(\"HEAD\", path)\n    if norm_ast(before) != norm_ast(after): bad_ast.append(path)\n    if directives(before) != directives(after): bad_directives.append(path)\nassert not bad_ast, f\"non-docstring AST changes: {bad_ast}\"\nassert not bad_directives, f\"directive/shebang changes: {bad_directives}\"' scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py scripts/main_health_report.py scripts/mutation_gate.py scripts/mutation_sandbox.py scripts/probe_rebar.py scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py scripts/release_guards.py scripts/retarget_jira_project.py scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py","dd_id":"python-prose-only","dd_text":"Require normalized non-docstring AST equivalence and exact directive/shebang preservation."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py tests/scripts/test_rebar_duration_probe.py tests/unit/test_release_guards.py tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py tests/scripts/test_check_import_walk.py::TestScriptsLeg::test_real_scripts_leg_passes","dd_id":"focused-tool-contracts","dd_text":"Exercise operational, mutation, release, duration, and CI-summary contracts."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD -- scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py scripts/main_health_report.py scripts/mutation_gate.py scripts/mutation_sandbox.py scripts/probe_rebar.py scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py scripts/release_guards.py scripts/retarget_jira_project.py scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"Reject whitespace errors in all declared paths."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"Run worktree lint and typecheck before review. Gerrit Verified supplies the repository-wide suite."}]},"source_event_uuids":["5377c128-0954-4e99-b188-5cb41f0b58f2","ef191d7b-1be2-4cd9-95a9-3726511817e4","25923bed-06df-434b-b250-08ad0a5e4ac7","dc5368c3-78f0-438c-aa95-10268f94a4b6","a3e54a0c-6924-42a0-89ec-9fff9aa3a86d","1c0e5c77-ae79-4720-9b11-e56082c9f6d0","81698f26-9881-44df-ada5-d9ff2367420d","d67a8864-296a-47b2-aa80-cd89cfea68d6","bd09e67d-b83d-4261-9fbd-5f97514f52c4","89b8f5d7-8128-41bf-b625-20a273389ec8","eae5b3b4-96b3-41c9-aec1-59586c6c8696